      "worked_solution": "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n\n \n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+⋯+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${(x-y)}^{8},$ we have  $a=x,$ $b=-y,$ $n=8.$ \n\nTherefore, the first three terms of ${(x-y)}^{8}$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x-y)}^{8} & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{8}{0}){(x)}^{8}{(-y)}^{0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{8}{1}){(x)}^{8-1}{(-y)}^{1}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{8}{2}){(x)}^{8-2}{(-y)}^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =1{(x)}^{8}+8{(x)}^{7}{(-y)}^{1}+28{(x)}^{6}{(-y)}^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & ={x}^{8}-8{x}^{7}y+28{x}^{6}{y}^{2}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
